1
00:00:01,335 --> 00:00:02,336
HI.

2
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:03,378
HI, YEAH, HI.

3
00:00:03,378 --> 00:00:04,755
I'M, UM, PHOEBE BUFFAY

4
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:06,882
AND I HAVE BABIES
COMING OUT OF ME.

5
00:00:06,882 --> 00:00:09,718
OKAY. HAVE YOU STARTED
HAVING CONTRACTIONS?

6
00:00:09,718 --> 00:00:11,679
NOT YET. I HEARD
THEY REALLY HURT.

7
00:00:11,679 --> 00:00:12,680
DO THEY HURT?

8
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:13,889
OH. WELL...

9
00:00:13,889 --> 00:00:16,517
OH, MY GOD.

10
00:00:16,517 --> 00:00:18,226
NOW, WHICH OF YOU
IS THE FATHER?

11
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:21,689
NO, NONE OF THEM ARE THE FATHER.
THE FATHER IS MY BROTHER.

12
00:00:21,689 --> 00:00:23,565
OKAY.

13
00:00:23,565 --> 00:00:24,984
I AM SO GOING TO MISS

14
00:00:24,984 --> 00:00:27,736
WATCHING YOU FREAK
PEOPLE OUT LIKE THAT.

15
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:29,070
( giggling )
OKAY, PHEEBS, LOOK, LOOK,

16
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:31,490
THIS IS FOR THE BABIES
TO LOOK AT SOMEDAY.

17
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:33,116
SO IS THERE ANYTHING
YOU WANT TO SAY--

18
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:34,702
YOU KNOW,
BEFORE IT ALL STARTS?

19
00:00:34,702 --> 00:00:37,204
OH, OKAY.
UM... HI, KIDS.

20
00:00:37,204 --> 00:00:39,957
UM, IT'S ME, AUNT PHOEBE.

21
00:00:39,957 --> 00:00:41,416
CAN'T WAIT TO SEE YOU.

22
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:43,126
PLEASE DON'T HURT ME.

23
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:47,339
HEY, WHAT TOOK
YOU GUYS SO LONG?

24
00:00:47,339 --> 00:00:49,048
YOUR CAB LEFT WHEN OURS DID.

25
00:00:51,886 --> 00:00:53,470
( clears throat )

26
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:55,389
WELL, WE HAD TO GO BACK
'CAUSE I FORGOT MY JACKET.

27
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:56,348
( chuckling ):
THAT'S RIGHT.

28
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:03,647
YOU... YOU'RE NOT
WEARING A JACKET.

29
00:01:03,647 --> 00:01:06,901
OH, MAN. I DID IT AGAIN.

30
00:01:06,901 --> 00:01:09,987
OKAY, SO SOMEONE HAS
TO CALL FRANK AND ALICE

31
00:01:09,987 --> 00:01:11,864
AND THEN MY MOM...
JOEY, WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

32
00:01:11,864 --> 00:01:14,033
WELL, I GOT TO GET
THE "BEFORE" SHOT.

33
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:22,791
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU ♪

34
00:01:22,791 --> 00:01:26,378
♪ LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

35
00:01:26,378 --> 00:01:28,756
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

36
00:01:28,756 --> 00:01:31,675
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

37
00:01:31,675 --> 00:01:36,095
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

38
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:38,432
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

39
00:01:38,432 --> 00:01:41,100
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

40
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:44,730
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

41
00:01:44,730 --> 00:01:46,815
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

42
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:49,443
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

43
00:01:49,443 --> 00:01:51,653
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

44
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:54,865
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

45
00:01:54,865 --> 00:01:58,368
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

46
00:02:07,419 --> 00:02:09,379
HI. PHEEBS? OKAY,
SO WE JUST SPOKE TO THE NURSE

47
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:11,548
AND THE REASON THAT
YOUR DOCTOR IS LATE

48
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,634
IS BECAUSE, UH,
SHE'S NOT COMING.

49
00:02:13,634 --> 00:02:17,471
WHAT?!
APPARENTLY, SHE FELL IN
THE SHOWER AND HIT HER HEAD.

50
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:20,682
OH, MY GOD.
SHE'S SO STUPID.

51
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:22,810
PHEEBS. PHEEBS,
IT'S GOING TO BE OKAY.

52
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:24,853
THAT'S EASY FOR YOU TO SAY.
I DON'T SEE THREE KIDS

53
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:26,730
COMING OUT OF YOUR VAGINA.

54
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,819
HONEY, LISTEN,
YOU KNOW WHAT?

55
00:02:31,819 --> 00:02:33,654
THE NURSE SAID THAT
THE DOCTOR IS WONDERFUL.

56
00:02:33,654 --> 00:02:35,572
YEAH, HE'S THE HEAD
OF THE DEPARTMENT.

57
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:36,698
( sighs ):
ALL RIGHT.

58
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:38,241
OOH. OH, DEAR GOD, SAVE ME.

59
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:39,910
WHAT?
I'M HAVING
MY FIRST CONTRACTION.

60
00:02:41,411 --> 00:02:43,038
OH, IT'S NOT BAD.
Chandler:
OKAY.

61
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:48,502
( deep voice ):
AND SO THE MIRACLE
OF BIRTH BEGINS AND...

62
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:49,544
( screaming )

63
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:50,963
HEY, ARE YOU OKAY?

64
00:02:50,963 --> 00:02:53,298
OOH. SOMETHING HURTS.

65
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,675
OOH, IT'S SYMPATHY PAINS.

66
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:57,011
OH, THAT'S SO SWEET.

67
00:02:57,011 --> 00:02:58,887
I DIDN'T KNOW
I CARED THAT MUCH.

68
00:03:01,849 --> 00:03:03,142
HELLO.
HI.

69
00:03:03,142 --> 00:03:05,226
PHOEBE, I'M DR. HARAD.

70
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:07,021
I'M GOING TO BE
DELIVERING YOUR BABIES.

71
00:03:07,021 --> 00:03:08,605
I WANT YOU TO KNOW YOU'RE
GOING TO BE IN GOOD HANDS.

72
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:10,398
I'VE BEEN DOING THIS
FOR A LONG TIME.

73
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:12,400
I'LL BE BACK IN A MINUTE
TO DO YOUR INTERNAL.

74
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,610
IN THE MEANTIME, JUST RELAX

75
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:15,445
BECAUSE EVERYTHING HERE
LOOKS GREAT.

76
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:17,739
AND, ALSO, I LOVE FONZIE.

77
00:03:21,451 --> 00:03:24,245
DID HE JUST SAY
HE LOVES FONZIE?

78
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:26,790
THAT'S WHAT
IT SOUNDED LIKE.

79
00:03:26,790 --> 00:03:29,084
ALL RIGHT.

80
00:03:29,084 --> 00:03:30,752
HEY!

81
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:32,295
( all yelling )

82
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:35,423
HEY, AM I LATE? AM I LATE?
NOBODY CAME OUT YET, RIGHT?

83
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:38,426
NO, NO, NO,
WE HAVEN'T STARTED YET.
WHERE'S ALICE?

84
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:40,428
UH, DELAWARE.
SHE'S ON HER WAY, THOUGH.

85
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:42,221
SO UNTIL SHE GETS HERE,
I'M GOING TO BE YOUR COACH.

86
00:03:42,221 --> 00:03:46,185
BUT DON'T WORRY-- SHE TOLD ME
ALL ABOUT THE "LA-MAZDA" STUFF.

87
00:03:46,185 --> 00:03:48,269
YEAH, THAT'S WHEN,
IF YOU GET THE BABIES OUT
BY THE END OF THE MONTH

88
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:50,105
THEY GIVE YOU
TWO PERCENT FINANCING.

89
00:03:51,356 --> 00:03:52,399
YEAH.

90
00:03:55,944 --> 00:03:58,613
MONICA, YOU'RE GOING
TO BE VERY PROUD OF ME.

91
00:03:58,613 --> 00:04:02,450
I JUST GOT US DATES WITH
TWO UNBELIEVABLY CUTE NURSES.

92
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:04,078
OH, MY.

93
00:04:05,162 --> 00:04:07,164
THEY ARE MALE NURSES.

94
00:04:07,164 --> 00:04:09,457
( chuckling ):
NOT IN MY HEAD.

95
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:12,335
ANYWAY, THEY WANT TO TAKE US OUT
SATURDAY NIGHT.

96
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:13,795
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

97
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:14,963
UM...

98
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,673
UM...

99
00:04:19,009 --> 00:04:20,969
I DON'T THINK SO.

100
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:23,222
WHAT? WHAT ARE
YOU TALKING ABOUT?

101
00:04:23,222 --> 00:04:24,973
YOU'RE THE ONE
WHO'S BEEN TELLING ME

102
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:27,308
TO GET OVER ROSS AND MOVE ON.

103
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:29,103
I'M MOVING ON,
AND YOU'RE MOVING ON WITH ME.

104
00:04:29,103 --> 00:04:31,146
COME ON. GIVE ME ONE GOOD REASON
WHY YOU DON'T WANT TO GO.

105
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:33,440
WELL, UM...

106
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:36,151
WHY DON'T YOU GIVE ME SOMETHING
THAT WOULD BE A GOOD REASON

107
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:38,528
AND THEN I'LL TELL YOU
IF IT'S TRUE?

108
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:43,491
WHAT?
HARDER THAN IT SOUNDS,
ISN'T IT?

109
00:04:43,491 --> 00:04:45,368
OKAY, YOU'RE COMING WITH ME,
I ALSO TOLD THEM THAT

110
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:46,661
IF WE'RE STILL HERE
WHEN THEY GET OFF

111
00:04:46,661 --> 00:04:47,871
THAT WE'LL GO DOWN
TO THE CAFETERIA

112
00:04:47,871 --> 00:04:49,039
AND GET SOME JELL-O WITH THEM.

113
00:04:49,039 --> 00:04:50,207
( deep voice ): YEP.

114
00:04:50,207 --> 00:04:53,376
THERE'S ALWAYS
ROOM FOR JELL-O.

115
00:04:56,171 --> 00:04:58,173
JOEY, HOW DO YOU MAKE
THAT DIRTY?

116
00:04:58,173 --> 00:04:59,925
AH, IT'S EASY.
YEAH, I CAN DO IT
WITH ANYTHING.

117
00:04:59,925 --> 00:05:01,843
WATCH. UH...

118
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:05,388
( deep voice ):
GRANDMA'S CHICKEN SALAD...

119
00:05:12,229 --> 00:05:14,273
ROSS! COME HERE.

120
00:05:14,273 --> 00:05:16,524
GET A SHOT OF THIS.

121
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:17,985
HEY, BABIES--

122
00:05:17,985 --> 00:05:19,694
THESE ARE THE HEADLINES
ON THE DAY YOU WERE BORN.

123
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:21,655
OKAY, NOW,
GIRL BABY, TURN AWAY

124
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:25,867
AND, BOY BABIES...
CHECK IT OUT, HUH?

125
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:28,996
THIS IS WHAT
NAKED WOMEN LOOKED LIKE,
THE MONTH YOU WERE BORN.

126
00:05:28,996 --> 00:05:32,874
ALL RIGHT, NOW LET'S DIVE
RIGHT INTO THE GOOD STUFF.

127
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:35,669
OKAY, I'M HAVING
ANOTHER ONE.

128
00:05:35,669 --> 00:05:36,837
THIS ONE DOESN'T HURT EITHER.

129
00:05:36,837 --> 00:05:38,922
OOH, YES, IT DOES. OW! OW!

130
00:05:38,922 --> 00:05:41,508
OW! OW!

131
00:05:41,508 --> 00:05:44,552
OOH!

132
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:46,513
OOH, I WAS KIND OF HOPING
THAT WAS IT.

133
00:05:49,266 --> 00:05:51,518
HEY, WHERE ARE MONICA
AND RACHEL ANYWAY?

134
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:54,855
A COUPLE OF NURSES ASKED THEM
OUT; MAYBE THEY'RE WITH THEM.

135
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,355
REALLY? MALE NURSES?

136
00:05:56,355 --> 00:05:59,943
YEAH. I WAS BUMMED, TOO.

137
00:05:59,943 --> 00:06:01,820
SO THEY'RE
GOING ON DATES?

138
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:02,821
WHEN?

139
00:06:02,821 --> 00:06:03,822
I THINK SATURDAY.

140
00:06:03,822 --> 00:06:05,991
( screaming )

141
00:06:05,991 --> 00:06:07,159
WHAT'S WITH HIM?

142
00:06:07,159 --> 00:06:08,785
UM, SYMPATHY PAINS.

143
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:10,411
I THOUGHT IT WAS
REALLY SWEET AT FIRST

144
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:14,041
BUT NOW I THINK HE'S JUST
TRYING TO STEAL MY THUNDER.

145
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:16,459
OKAY.
OKAY.

146
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:18,753
LET'S SEE WHAT WE GOT HERE.

147
00:06:18,753 --> 00:06:21,965
OH, YOU KNOW,
FONZIE DATED TRIPLETS.

148
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:26,136
THIS FONZIE PERSON
YOU KEEP REFERRING TO--

149
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:28,763
IS THAT, UH... IS
THAT ANOTHER DOCTOR?

150
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:30,098
OH, NO, NO.

151
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:34,393
FONZIE IS THE NICKNAME
OF ARTHUR FONZARELLI.

152
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:35,394
THE FONZ.

153
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:39,274
ALL RIGHT.

154
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:45,572
IT'S NOT THAT WEIRD,
IS IT?

155
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:47,532
IT'S VERY WEIRD.

156
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:51,995
I DON'T WANT SOME GUY DOWN THERE
TELLING ME I'M "DILATED-AMUNDO."

157
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:57,792
TO BE FAIR, HE DOESN'T SEEM
TO BE IMPERSONATING FONZIE...

158
00:06:57,792 --> 00:07:00,379
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?!

159
00:07:00,379 --> 00:07:02,881
WHY ARE YOU DEFENDING HIM?
JUST GET ME ANOTHER DOCTOR--

160
00:07:02,881 --> 00:07:06,509
ONE WHO IS NOT CRAZY
AND DOES NOT "FONZIE."

161
00:07:06,509 --> 00:07:07,635
AGAIN, IT'S NOT THAT HE...

162
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:08,595
OH! OH!

163
00:07:14,893 --> 00:07:16,978
OH, HEY,
THERE-THERE YOU ARE.

164
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:19,522
LISTEN, I-I THINK
THAT THERE IS SOMETHING
THAT YOU SHOULD KNOW.

165
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:21,608
OH, IS THIS ABOUT YOU...
YOU DATING THE NURSE?

166
00:07:21,608 --> 00:07:24,819
YEAH. JOEY ALREADY TOLD ME,
AND I AM SO, SO FINE.

167
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:26,654
I MEAN, YOU AND I--
WE'RE JUST, YOU KNOW,
WE'RE NOTHING.

168
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:29,241
WE'RE JUST...
EH, GOOFING AROUND.

169
00:07:31,952 --> 00:07:34,079
UM, ACTUALLY I WAS
ABOUT TO TELL YOU

170
00:07:34,079 --> 00:07:36,290
THAT I WAS-I WAS
GOING TO GET OUT OF IT

171
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:37,958
BUT, HEY, IF WE'RE
JUST GOOFING AROUND

172
00:07:37,958 --> 00:07:40,168
THEN, UH, MAYBE I WILL 
GO OUT WITH HIM.

173
00:07:40,168 --> 00:07:42,296
FINE. MAYBE I WILL, TOO.

174
00:07:44,756 --> 00:07:47,842
HEY. YOU GUYS. LOOK WHAT I FOUND
IN THE... GIIIFT SHOP!

175
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:51,221
OH! OW! GET UP! GET UP!

176
00:07:56,059 --> 00:07:57,477
OKAY, PHEEBS?
YEAH.

177
00:07:57,477 --> 00:07:59,104
THIS IS DR. OBERMAN.

178
00:07:59,104 --> 00:08:02,441
HE HAS NO STRONG
FEELINGS ABOUT FONZIE

179
00:08:02,441 --> 00:08:06,194
OR ANY OF THE 
HAPPY DAYS GANG.

180
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:09,781
HI. AND YOU'RE GOING
INTO WHAT GRADE?

181
00:08:09,781 --> 00:08:12,367
I'M ACTUALLY
A FIRST-YEAR RESIDENT,
BUT I GET THAT A LOT.

182
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:13,368
YOU SEE, I GRADUATED EARLY...

183
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:14,702
UH-HUH, ME, TOO.

184
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:17,538
ROSS, MAYBE I SHOULD
HAVE SPECIFIED

185
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:20,292
THAT I'D BE NEEDING
A GROWN-UP DOCTOR.

186
00:08:20,292 --> 00:08:22,043
OH, NO, REALLY,
I'M FULLY QUALIFIED TO...

187
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:23,253
SHH! DOOGIE, SHH!

188
00:08:25,672 --> 00:08:27,590
DOESN'T ANYBODY
UNDERSTAND THAT I'M

189
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:30,593
GOING TO BE HAVING
BABIES SOON? HUH?!

190
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:32,762
GO! GO, LITTLE BOY, GO!

191
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:38,935
OH, YOU MADE HIM CRY.

192
00:08:43,898 --> 00:08:45,900
MR. TRIBBIANI,
I'M AFRAID

193
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,403
YOU'VE GOT
KIDNEY STONES.

194
00:08:48,403 --> 00:08:50,905
UH... WELL, WHAT ELSE
COULD IT BE?

195
00:08:50,905 --> 00:08:54,075
IT'S KIDNEY STONES.

196
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:55,076
OR...

197
00:08:55,076 --> 00:08:56,870
KIDNEY STONES.

198
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:02,792
ALL RIGHT,
YOU'RE GETTING THERE.

199
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:05,295
OH, AND, YOU KNOW THESE BABIES
ARE VERY, VERY LUCKY.

200
00:09:05,295 --> 00:09:06,587
THEY ARE? WHY?

201
00:09:06,587 --> 00:09:07,964
THEY HAVE THE HONOR
OF BEING BORN

202
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:09,883
ON THE FONZ'S HALF-BIRTHDAY.

203
00:09:12,177 --> 00:09:14,388
HAPPY BIRTHDAY.

204
00:09:14,388 --> 00:09:16,639
JUST TO CLARIFY...

205
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:18,808
I'M NOT FONZIE.

206
00:09:26,774 --> 00:09:28,235
HONEY, YOU KNOW,
I JUST GOT TO TELL YOU.

207
00:09:28,235 --> 00:09:29,903
I THINK THIS IS
SUCH A TERRIFIC THING

208
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:31,654
YOU'RE HAVING THESE
BABIES FOR FRANK AND ALICE.

209
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:33,781
NO, IT IS.
YEAH.

210
00:09:33,781 --> 00:09:35,409
CAN I TELL YOU
A LITTLE SECRET?

211
00:09:35,409 --> 00:09:37,035
YEAH.

212
00:09:37,035 --> 00:09:39,454
I WANT TO KEEP ONE.

213
00:09:43,208 --> 00:09:45,793
OH, I'M GOING TO
BE ON THE NEWS.

214
00:09:49,464 --> 00:09:51,716
OKAY, PHOEBE. HONEY,
YOU'VE GOT TO BE KIDDING.

215
00:09:51,716 --> 00:09:53,801
YOU KNOW YOU CAN'T KEEP
ONE OF THESE BABIES.

216
00:09:53,801 --> 00:09:56,012
WHY NOT? MAYBE I CAN;
YOU DON'T KNOW.

217
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:58,515
YES, YES, I DO KNOW--
FRANK AND ALICE ARE GOING

218
00:09:58,515 --> 00:10:00,267
TO WANT TO KEEP ALL
OF THEIR CHILDREN.

219
00:10:00,267 --> 00:10:03,186
MAYBE NOT, YOU KNOW?

220
00:10:03,186 --> 00:10:05,397
SERIOUSLY-- THREE BABIES
ARE A HANDFUL.

221
00:10:05,397 --> 00:10:06,814
MAYBE THEY'RE, YOU KNOW,
LOOKING FOR A CHANCE

222
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:09,692
TO UNLOAD ONE OF THEM.

223
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:11,528
I'D HATE TO MISS
AN OPPORTUNITY

224
00:10:11,528 --> 00:10:13,572
JUST 'CAUSE I DIDN'T ASK.

225
00:10:15,323 --> 00:10:18,034
PHOEBE, NO. THIS IS...
THIS IS INSANE.

226
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:19,369
OH, JUST ASK HIM.

227
00:10:19,369 --> 00:10:21,246
WHA...? ME?

228
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:22,830
I CAN'T ASK HIM.

229
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:25,208
DO YOU HAVE ANY IDEA
HOW INAPPROPRIATE THAT WOULD BE?

230
00:10:27,377 --> 00:10:29,754
ALL I'M SAYING IS JUST
TALK TO FRANK, OKAY?

231
00:10:29,754 --> 00:10:31,881
JUST... YOU KNOW,
FEEL HIM OUT.

232
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:33,550
NO. FORGET IT.
I AM NOT GOING TO ASK FRANK

233
00:10:33,550 --> 00:10:35,135
TO GIVE YOU ONE OF HIS KIDS.

234
00:10:36,553 --> 00:10:38,096
YOU'RE RIGHT.

235
00:10:42,434 --> 00:10:43,768
( sighs )

236
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,853
TELL HIM IT'S FOR YOU.

237
00:10:48,106 --> 00:10:49,941
FEELING A LITTLE
BETTER, SWEETIE?

238
00:10:49,941 --> 00:10:51,943
WELL, MAYBE A LITTLE.

239
00:10:51,943 --> 00:10:53,778
I WISH YOU HADN'T
SEEN ME THROW UP.

240
00:10:55,322 --> 00:10:56,406
ME, TOO.

241
00:10:58,617 --> 00:11:00,368
HEY. I JUST HEARD.

242
00:11:00,368 --> 00:11:01,369
WHAT'S UP?

243
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:03,371
KIDNEY STONES.

244
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:08,668
NOW, ORDINARILY, MR. TRIBBIANI

245
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:10,795
WE TRY TO BREAK THE STONES UP
WITH SHOCK WAVES

246
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:13,173
BUT THEY'RE TOO CLOSE
TO THE BLADDER NOW

247
00:11:13,173 --> 00:11:15,674
WHICH MEANS WE CAN EITHER
WAIT FOR YOU TO PASS THEM

248
00:11:15,674 --> 00:11:17,469
OR ELSE GO UP THE URETHRA.

249
00:11:17,469 --> 00:11:20,388
WHOA-HO!

250
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:22,098
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

251
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:23,891
NOTHING IS GOING UP, OKAY?

252
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:26,645
"UP"-- "UP" IS
NOT AN OPTION.

253
00:11:26,645 --> 00:11:27,979
WHAT'S A URETHRA?

254
00:11:30,398 --> 00:11:31,566
( whispering )

255
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:32,942
ARE YOU CRAZY?!

256
00:11:36,446 --> 00:11:38,198
SO DID YOU ASK HIM?

257
00:11:38,198 --> 00:11:40,241
NO. I HAVEN'T HAD A CHANCE
TO BE ALONE WITH HIM YET.

258
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:42,035
WELL, I'M KIND OF
ON A CLOCK HERE.

259
00:11:43,662 --> 00:11:45,038
( chuckling )

260
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:47,040
OH, FONZIE.

261
00:11:50,001 --> 00:11:52,420
YOU KNOW WHO I
ALWAYS LIKED? MORK.

262
00:11:56,007 --> 00:11:57,634
UNDO IT, UNDO IT, UNDO IT.

263
00:11:59,927 --> 00:12:02,013
FONZIE MET MORK.

264
00:12:02,013 --> 00:12:04,391
MORK FROZE FONZIE.

265
00:12:04,391 --> 00:12:07,519
YEAH. UM...

266
00:12:07,519 --> 00:12:09,229
YES, BUT...

267
00:12:09,229 --> 00:12:13,525
FONZIE WAS
ALREADY COOL...

268
00:12:13,525 --> 00:12:17,237
SO HE WASN'T
HURT, RIGHT?

269
00:12:17,237 --> 00:12:18,697
YEAH, THAT'S RIGHT.

270
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:23,034
HEY.
HI.

271
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:25,953
HOW YOU DOING?
OKAY. THE DOCTOR
SAYS ANY MINUTE KNOW.

272
00:12:25,953 --> 00:12:27,539
HEY, YOU KNOW

273
00:12:27,539 --> 00:12:29,708
ALICE IS GOING
TO BE HERE SO SOON.

274
00:12:29,708 --> 00:12:33,086
YOU COULDN'T JUST, LIKE,
DO ME A FAVOR AND, LIKE...

275
00:12:33,086 --> 00:12:36,506
LIKE-LIKE HOLD THEM IN?

276
00:12:36,506 --> 00:12:38,633
SORRY, FRANK. I'M KIND OF
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE LAST FAVOR

277
00:12:38,633 --> 00:12:41,344
YOU ASKED ME TO DO.

278
00:12:41,344 --> 00:12:42,345
HEY.

279
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:43,930
HI.
RACHEL...

280
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:46,433
UH, MONICA, THIS IS DAN,
ONE OF THE GUYS WE'RE GOING

281
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:47,892
TO BE GOING OUT WITH
ON SATURDAY.

282
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:49,269
UH, DAN, MONICA.

283
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:50,604
NICE TO MEET YOU.

284
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:54,815
HELLO, DAN.

285
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:56,693
I'M REALLY LOOKING FORWARD
TO SATURDAY NIGHT--

286
00:12:56,693 --> 00:12:58,236
REALLY, REALLY!

287
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:03,408
SO, DAN...

288
00:13:03,408 --> 00:13:06,077
NURSE, NOT A DOCTOR, HUH?

289
00:13:06,077 --> 00:13:07,704
KIND OF GIRLIE, ISN'T IT?

290
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:13,042
CHANDLER...
NO, THAT'S OKAY;
I'M JUST DOING THIS

291
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:15,794
TO PUT MYSELF THROUGH
MEDICAL SCHOOL.

292
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:18,131
OH.

293
00:13:18,131 --> 00:13:21,259
AND IT DIDN'T FEEL SO GIRLIE
DURING THE GULF WAR.

294
00:13:21,259 --> 00:13:22,761
SURE.

295
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:29,016
AND, LISTEN, THANKS FOR DOING
THAT FOR US BY THE WAY.

296
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:35,022
SO WHY WAIT TILL SATURDAY?
ARE YOU FREE TOMORROW?

297
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:37,024
SURE. I'LL GET SOMEBODY
TO COVER MY SHIFT.

298
00:13:37,024 --> 00:13:38,859
AW, GREAT.

299
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:40,987
HEY, UH, HOW ABOUT IT--
YOU AND ME, SATURDAY NIGHT?

300
00:13:40,987 --> 00:13:43,030
NO.
ALL RIGHT. VERY GOOD.

301
00:13:45,283 --> 00:13:48,286
OOH, THIS IS A BIG ONE.

302
00:13:48,286 --> 00:13:50,789
( screams )

303
00:13:50,789 --> 00:13:53,750
OH! GET THESE THINGS
OUT OF ME!

304
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:55,669
BREATHE...

305
00:13:55,669 --> 00:13:57,378
BREATHE THROUGH THE PAIN.

306
00:13:57,378 --> 00:14:00,674
( wheezing )

307
00:14:00,674 --> 00:14:01,966
I WANT THE DRUGS, ROSS!

308
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,217
I WANT THE DRUGS!

309
00:14:03,217 --> 00:14:05,386
I DO, TOO! I DO, TOO!

310
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:08,264
( both screaming )

311
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:10,308
YEAH, I LOVE YOU.

312
00:14:10,308 --> 00:14:12,226
OKAY. BYE.

313
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:14,061
HI.
HI.

314
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:17,231
THAT WAS ALICE'S MOM. SHE SAID
THAT SHE LEFT FIVE HOURS AGO.

315
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:19,609
SHE SHOULD BE HERE BY NOW.
OH, HONEY, DON'T WORRY.

316
00:14:19,609 --> 00:14:20,735
SHE'S GOING
TO MAKE IT ON TIME.

317
00:14:20,735 --> 00:14:22,570
YEAH.
YEAH.

318
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:25,699
SO, FRANK... THREE BABIES.

319
00:14:25,699 --> 00:14:28,117
WHOO! THAT JUST SEEMS
LIKE A LOT, HUH?

320
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:30,077
( chuckling ):
NOT TO ME.

321
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:33,039
YEAH, FAIR ENOUGH.

322
00:14:37,711 --> 00:14:39,420
OKAY, YOU'RE
TEN CENTIMETERS.

323
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:41,422
TIME TO START HAVING
SOME BABIES.

324
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:43,424
I WANT ONLY THE FATHER
IN HERE, PLEASE.

325
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:46,636
WE LOVE YOU.
GOOD LUCK.
LOVE YOU.

326
00:14:46,636 --> 00:14:47,679
BYE, DAN.

327
00:14:47,679 --> 00:14:48,680
UH, BYE, MONICA.

328
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,473
UH... BYE ( babbling ).

329
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:55,978
ALL RIGHT. I NEED A CLAMP,
A STERILE TOWEL AND CHANNEL 31.

330
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:57,271
WHAT IS THAT?

331
00:14:57,271 --> 00:14:59,899
♪ Sunday, Monday, Happy Days ♪

332
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,401
♪ Tuesday, Wednesday,
Happy Days... ♪

333
00:15:01,401 --> 00:15:03,277
OH, MY GOD!
OH, NO, NO, NO.

334
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:06,906
IT'S A GOOD ONE.
FONZIE PLAYS THE BONGOS.

335
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:09,492
ALL RIGHT, YOU READY?
IT'S TIME TO TRY PUSHING.

336
00:15:09,492 --> 00:15:11,494
ARE YOU READY?
IT'S TIME TO TRY PEEING.

337
00:15:15,665 --> 00:15:16,957
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT,
WAIT, WAIT! WAIT!

338
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:20,086
IT'S ALMOST TIME
TO TRY PEEING.

339
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:23,590
NOW, PUSH. THAT'S IT, PUSH.

340
00:15:23,590 --> 00:15:24,883
NOW, JUST CONCENTRATE
ON PUSHING.

341
00:15:24,883 --> 00:15:26,300
YEAH, HERE WE GO.
I SEE THE HEAD.

342
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,010
YES! IT HAS A HEAD!

343
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:29,763
ALL RIGHT.

344
00:15:29,763 --> 00:15:31,598
THAT'S IT.
KEEP PUSHING. COME ON.

345
00:15:31,598 --> 00:15:33,892
I CAN'T BELIEVE THERE'S SOMEBODY
COMING OUT OF YOU RIGHT NOW.

346
00:15:33,892 --> 00:15:37,103
THERE'S SOMEBODY COMING
OUT OF YOU, AND HE'S, HE'S...

347
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:39,146
THAT'S MY SON!
ALL RIGHT.

348
00:15:39,146 --> 00:15:41,399
( baby crying )

349
00:15:41,399 --> 00:15:43,484
HERE'S YOUR FIRST BABY.

350
00:15:46,112 --> 00:15:47,947
YES!

351
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,783
YES! WE GOT
A BABY BOY!

352
00:15:49,783 --> 00:15:51,409
( all cheering )

353
00:15:51,409 --> 00:15:53,620
FRANK, JR., JR.!

354
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:55,455
OH! HOW DOES HE LOOK?
HOW DOES HE LOOK?

355
00:15:55,455 --> 00:15:56,955
SO GROSS!

356
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:02,503
OKAY, YOU READY
TO PUSH AGAIN?

357
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:05,673
OH, I ALREADY HAD A BABY--
LEAVE ME ALONE.

358
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:07,049
OKAY, OKAY, COME ON.
YOU CAN DO IT.

359
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:09,469
YOU CAN DO IT.

360
00:16:09,469 --> 00:16:11,638
( screams )

361
00:16:11,638 --> 00:16:13,598
( screams )

362
00:16:15,767 --> 00:16:18,352
YEAH! HA-HA!

363
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:21,856
LITTLE LESLIE'S HERE!
WE GOT ANOTHER ONE!

364
00:16:21,856 --> 00:16:24,609
OH, MY GOD.
I CAN'T BELIEVE I HAVE...

365
00:16:24,609 --> 00:16:26,444
TWO CHILDREN.

366
00:16:26,444 --> 00:16:29,280
HOW SCARY IS THAT?

367
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:34,577
COME ON, LITTLE CHANDLER,
IT'S TIME TO BE BORN.

368
00:16:34,577 --> 00:16:36,203
COME ON, LITTLE CHANDLER.

369
00:16:36,203 --> 00:16:38,539
YEP. ALL RIGHT,
HE'S COMING.
COME ON.

370
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:39,916
HE'S COMING. HE'S COMING.

371
00:16:39,916 --> 00:16:43,878
( crying )

372
00:16:43,878 --> 00:16:45,505
HEY, WHERE'S HIS THING?

373
00:16:50,008 --> 00:16:51,636
CHANDLER IS A GIRL!

374
00:16:53,596 --> 00:16:57,266
OH, GOD,
KINDERGARTEN FLASHBACK.

375
00:16:57,266 --> 00:16:59,226
WELL, THEY MUST HAVE READ
THE SONOGRAM WRONG

376
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:01,562
'CAUSE THEY-'CAUSE THEY
THOUGHT IT WAS A BOY

377
00:17:01,562 --> 00:17:03,523
BUT CHANDLER'S A GIRL;
CHANDLER'S A GIRL!

378
00:17:03,523 --> 00:17:06,024
OKAY! KEEP SAYING IT!

379
00:17:06,024 --> 00:17:07,777
AM I TOO LATE?

380
00:17:07,777 --> 00:17:09,863
NO, NO. EVERYTHING'S OKAY;
EVERYBODY'S HEALTHY.

381
00:17:09,863 --> 00:17:12,907
THERE'S 30 FINGERS
AND 30 TOES.

382
00:17:12,907 --> 00:17:14,116
WE HAVE OUR BABIES?

383
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,493
YEAH...

384
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:17,662
OH. WE HAVE OUR BABIES.

385
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:33,803
OH, MY GOD.

386
00:17:33,803 --> 00:17:35,722
YOU DID IT, MAN.

387
00:17:37,015 --> 00:17:39,017
WOULD YOU LIKE
TO SEE THEM?

388
00:17:41,895 --> 00:17:44,230
THEY'RE SO SMALL...

389
00:17:51,612 --> 00:17:52,613
SO I'LL CALL YOU TOMORROW.

390
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:54,032
GREAT.

391
00:17:58,244 --> 00:18:02,040
SO ARE YOU REALLY GOING
TO GO OUT WITH THAT NURSE MAN?

392
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:04,333
WELL, YOU AND I ARE
JUST "GOOFING AROUND"

393
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:07,545
AND I THOUGHT, "WHY NOT
JUST GOOF AROUND WITH HIM?"

394
00:18:10,048 --> 00:18:11,716
YOU KNOW, I DON'T KNOW
IF YOU'VE EVER LOOKED UP

395
00:18:11,716 --> 00:18:14,468
THE TERM "GOOFING AROUND"
IN THE DICTIONARY.

396
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:15,636
WELL, I HAVE.

397
00:18:15,636 --> 00:18:17,764
AND THE TECHNICAL

398
00:18:17,764 --> 00:18:20,725
DEFINITION IS...

399
00:18:20,725 --> 00:18:22,142
TWO FRIENDS...

400
00:18:22,142 --> 00:18:25,688
WHO CARE A LOT
ABOUT EACH OTHER

401
00:18:25,688 --> 00:18:28,274
AND HAVE... AMAZING SEX...

402
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:35,489
AND JUST WANT TO SPEND
MORE TIME TOGETHER, YOU KNOW?

403
00:18:35,489 --> 00:18:37,366
BUT, IF YOU HAVE
THIS NEWFANGLED DICTIONARY

404
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:39,285
THAT GETS YOU MAD AT ME,
THEN WE HAVE TO, YOU KNOW,

405
00:18:39,285 --> 00:18:42,246
GET YOU
MY ORIGINAL DICTIONARY.

406
00:18:45,165 --> 00:18:47,835
I AM SO BAD AT THIS.

407
00:18:47,835 --> 00:18:50,088
I THINK YOU'RE BETTER
THAN YOU THINK YOU ARE.

408
00:18:50,088 --> 00:18:51,129
REALLY?

409
00:18:51,129 --> 00:18:53,091
OKAY. SO IF...

410
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:54,092
KNOW WHEN TO STOP.

411
00:18:54,092 --> 00:18:55,551
I SENSED THAT I SHOULD STOP.

412
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:57,011
MM-HMM.

413
00:18:57,011 --> 00:18:58,596
SO, WE'RE OKAY?

414
00:18:58,596 --> 00:19:01,223
YEAH. ALL RIGHT, I'M
GOING TO GO TELL DAN

415
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:02,976
THAT IT'S NOT
GOING TO HAPPEN.

416
00:19:06,437 --> 00:19:08,106
DON'T DO THE DANCE.
RIGHT.

417
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:14,695
I THINK
YOU'RE MY FAVORITE.

418
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:15,905
WHICH ONE DO YOU HAVE?

419
00:19:15,905 --> 00:19:17,239
I DON'T CARE.

420
00:19:19,659 --> 00:19:20,701
HI.

421
00:19:20,701 --> 00:19:22,620
HEY.

422
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:24,455
SO FRANK AND ALICE
WANTED ME TO TELL YOU

423
00:19:24,455 --> 00:19:26,082
THEY'RE STILL OUTSIDE,
MAKING PHONE CALLS.

424
00:19:26,082 --> 00:19:27,500
OH. BUT, UM, I MEAN

425
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:30,086
DID YOU TALK TO THEM
ABOUT... YOU KNOW?

426
00:19:30,086 --> 00:19:31,629
YEAH.

427
00:19:31,629 --> 00:19:34,256
UM...

428
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:35,967
( sighs ):
NO, HONEY.

429
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:38,136
OH, OKAY.

430
00:19:40,178 --> 00:19:41,555
IT WAS A LONG SHOT.

431
00:19:44,976 --> 00:19:46,769
HEY, YOU GUYS,
CAN I JUST HAVE

432
00:19:46,769 --> 00:19:48,771
LIKE, A SECOND ALONE
WITH THE BABIES?

433
00:19:48,771 --> 00:19:49,897
OH, YEAH, SURE.

434
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:51,024
YEAH.

435
00:19:51,024 --> 00:19:52,650
( sniffling )

436
00:19:55,153 --> 00:19:57,822
( crying softly )

437
00:20:07,832 --> 00:20:10,250
( door closes )

438
00:20:11,544 --> 00:20:13,253
SO HERE YOU ARE.

439
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:16,340
SEEMS LIKE YESTERDAY
I WAS TALKING TO YOU

440
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:18,216
IN THAT LITTLE PETRI DISH.

441
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,559
EVERYONE SAID
LABOR WAS THE HARDEST THING

442
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:28,268
I'D EVER HAVE TO DO,
BUT THEY WERE WRONG.

443
00:20:28,268 --> 00:20:29,603
THIS IS.

444
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:37,153
WELL, I HAD THE MOST FUN
WITH YOU GUYS...

445
00:20:37,153 --> 00:20:40,698
AND I WISH I COULD TAKE YOU HOME
AND SEE YOU EVERY DAY...

446
00:20:43,826 --> 00:20:46,453
OKAY, I'LL SETTLE FOR BEING
YOUR FAVORITE AUNT.

447
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:51,959
I KNOW ALICE'S SISTER HAS
A POOL, BUT YOU LIVED IN ME.

448
00:20:57,548 --> 00:21:00,718
OKAY, SO WE'RE COOL.

449
00:21:00,718 --> 00:21:02,428
YEAH, WE'RE GOING TO BE GREAT.

450
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:04,346
OKAY?

451
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:05,639
LITTLE HIGH FIVES?

452
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:07,683
AH! AH! AH!

453
00:21:08,935 --> 00:21:10,144
OH...

454
00:21:11,729 --> 00:21:14,148
( baby cries )

455
00:21:16,109 --> 00:21:18,903
WELL, IF YOU'RE GOING TO CRY...

456
00:21:18,903 --> 00:21:21,155
( sobbing softly )

457
00:21:34,043 --> 00:21:37,880
PHOEBE, WE ARE SO PROUD
OF YOU; YOU'RE AMAZING.

458
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:39,173
I KNOW.

459
00:21:40,925 --> 00:21:42,635
DOES IT REALLY HURT
AS BAD AS THEY SAY?

460
00:21:42,635 --> 00:21:44,887
YEAH. YOU WON'T BE ABLE
TO TAKE IT.

461
00:21:47,098 --> 00:21:49,391
SO, NOW THAT LITTLE CHANDLER
TURNED OUT TO BE A GIRL

462
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:50,810
WHAT ARE THEY
GOING TO NAME HER?

463
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:52,561
THEY'RE GOING TO
CALL HER CHANDLER.

464
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:56,274
KIND OF A MASCULINE NAME,
DON'T YOU THINK?

465
00:21:57,608 --> 00:21:58,985
WORKS ON YOU.

